  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Orange Corners Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">An initiative of the Kingdom of the Netherlands, Orange Corners Bangladesh taps into the potential of Bangladeshi youth, equipping them with skills, finances, and resources to enable them to turn their
smart ideas into sustainable businesses. The Orange Corners programme in Bangladesh is divided into three phases: Pre-Incubation, Incubation, and Post-Incubation.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of this program is to create opportunities for entrepreneurship and employability for Bangladeshi youth, so they can shape their own future through increased awareness of and expertise in entrepreneurship, development of soft skills and technical skills, and increased access to finance in order to contribute to a prosperous, sustainable and inclusive society. 

The specific objectives of this action are: (1) Bangladeshi youth participate in solving local challenges; (2) increased employment and entrepreneurship opportunities for Bangladeshi youth; (3) increased access to finance for Bangladeshi youth; (4) the private sector actively supports youth entrepreneurship and employment; and (5) ensuring gender equity with the program activities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The target group will be Bangladeshi university graduates and young professionals aged between 18 to 35 years, of which 50% are female, who have an affinity with active citizenship and entrepreneurship, and are passionate about solving social problems with innovative solutions</narrative>
  </description>
